  "emoji": "🎧",
  "summary": "Start the final week by listening to three real recordings, a radio weather bulletin, a station announcement and a voicemail, and catch the numbers, times, names and connectors that carry the key facts.",
  "intro": "The last week of the course begins with مُرَاجَعَةُ الِاسْتِمَاع, a listening review. Mr Karim plays three تَسْجِيلَات (recordings): a نَشْرَةُ الطَّقْس (weather bulletin) on the radio, an إِعْلَان (announcement) at the station and a رِسَالَة صَوْتِيَّة (voicemail). The secret of listening is not to catch every word but the key facts: numbers, times, names and connectors like لٰكِنْ (but) and أَمَّا (as for). Past weather comes with كَانَ and the -an ending, كَانَ الْجَوُّ غَائِمًا أَمْسِ (it was cloudy yesterday), and time words like أَمْسِ, غَدًا and مُنْذُ tell you when. In fast speech, words run together: مِنَ الرَّصِيفِ (mina r-raṣīf, from the platform) and عَنِ التَّأْخِير (ʿani t-taʾkhīr, for the delay). If you miss something, ask: هَلْ يُمْكِنُ أَنْ تُكَرِّرَ بِوُضُوح؟ (could you repeat that clearly?).",
  "objectives": [
    "Pick out the key facts in a recording: numbers, times, names and places",
    "Understand a weather bulletin that says what the weather was like with كَانَ and what it will be like with سَيَكُونُ",
    "Follow a station announcement: the train, the platform (الرَّصِيف), the time and the delay",
    "Hear the helping vowel in fast speech, as in مِنَ الرَّصِيفِ and عَنِ التَّأْخِير, and ask someone to repeat clearly"
